{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966480,"nonce":"zf5lEcalSPSVn+5N/R7ym0OuPNI=","title":"Web: text alignment and decoration width disagreed with measurement","message":"On web, centred text and underline/strikethrough widths did not match\nwhat the measurer reported.\n\nThe font registry's negative cache was the cause. `preload_generic_styles`\nran before the font bytes had loaded and cached \"not found\" for every\ngeneric family and weight combination; later preloads then hit the stale\nnegative entries and never resolved the real font, so the measurer and\nthe renderer used different metrics.\n\nFixed in 990937c3: `invalidate_generic_cache()` clears negative entries\nbefore preload re-runs after a font load. JetBrains Mono and Fira Code\nwere also added to the monospace fallback name list.\n\nCarried over from the root `backlog.md`, which this issue replaces.","files":null}]}